{{also|Dominion}}

==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=dominion (disambiguation)|dominion}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|dem}}
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|dominion}}, from {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|dominion}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|dominio}}, equiv. to {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|dominium||lordship, right of ownership}}, from {{m|la|dominus||lord}}, from {{m|la|domus||house}}. See [[domain]], [[demain]], [[demesne]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-dominion.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪnjən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Power or the use of power; [[sovereignty]] over something; [[stewardship]], [[supremacy]].
#* Bible, Daniel iv. 34
#*: I praised and honoured him that liveth forever, whose '''dominion''' is an everlasting dominion.
#* Jowett
#*: To choose between '''dominion''' or slavery.
# [[predominance]]; [[ascendancy]]
#* Dryden
#*: Objects placed foremost ought {{...}} have '''dominion''' over things confused and transient.
# {{lb|en|sometimes|figurative}} A [[kingdom]], [[nation]], or other [[sphere of influence]]; [[govern]]ed [[territory]].
#: ''the '''dominions''' of a king''
#: ''the '''dominion''' of the passions''
# {{lb|en|historical}} One of the [[dependencies]] of the [[British Empire]] given self-government and eventually independence, such as Canada, Newfoundland, or the Irish Free State.
# {{lb|en|Biblical tradition}} An order of [[angel]] in Christian [[angelology]], ranked above [[angel]]s and below [[throne]]s.
#* Bible, Colossians 1:16
#*: By him were all things created {{...}} whether they be thrones, or '''dominions''', or principalities, or powers.

